        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-78204",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ generate a circle of radius $1$ centered at the point $(3,2)?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +a,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +b,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have a circle of radius $1$ centered at the point $(3,2).$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"
      },
